From 986eae29c17a32e396505209e35c2a18646ad7c9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 17:00:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(ci): land upstream syncs through a PR now that main
 enforces CI for admins [daveey]

daveey/hermes main has enforce_admins=true: GitHub refuses any direct push
whose exact sha lacks a green "All required checks pass (v2)". The gate's
land() pushed the tested head (which carries only the upstream-sync check)
or a fresh merge commit (no checks) straight to main, and reported the
GH006 refusal as "NOT YET: main moved during publication", so it would
have retried forever on a misdiagnosis.

land() now opens (or reuses) a PR from the staged sync/upstream-<head>
branch itself, reads the required check on exactly that head
(pending/missing = NOT_YET, failure/cancelled = REFUSED) and then merges
it as a merge commit pinned to that head, without an admin override.
Any GH006 / GH013 / protected-branch / base-branch-policy refusal is
REFUSED with GitHub's own message.
